# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows clone rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF, and the next edit produces a whole-file diff that buries the
# real change. It also puts the UTF-8 repair in app/index.tsx at risk: a tool
# that rewrites a file it believes is mis-encoded can silently undo it.
#
# This governs files from here on. Already-committed files are left alone —
# renormalising the whole tree is a separate, deliberate act (`git add
# --renormalize .`), not a side effect of adding this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico  binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks  binary
